%% How a human uses the platform end to end. From alert to reviewing the
%% clip, every camera-data access is permission-checked, signed, and audited.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor OP as Operator
    participant APP as Dashboard (SPA)
    participant API as API Gateway + Lambda
    participant COG as Cognito
    participant SNOW as Snowflake
    participant S3 as S3 (video)
    participant AUD as access_audit

    OP->>APP: sign in
    APP->>COG: authenticate
    COG-->>APP: token (role, tenant)

    Note over OP,SNOW: Morning check
    APP->>API: get fleet status + telemetry
    API->>SNOW: query (WH_BI, row policy applies)
    SNOW-->>APP: device health, latest events

    Note over OP,S3: Alert -> review footage
    API-->>OP: push/email alert (PPE violation)
    OP->>APP: open event
    APP->>API: request clip for media_object
    API->>API: check role + tenant (may view PII?)
    alt allowed
        API->>S3: create short-lived signed URL
        API->>AUD: write access_audit row
        API-->>APP: signed URL (expires in minutes)
        APP->>S3: fetch clip directly
    else not allowed
        API-->>APP: 403, event shown without footage
    end

    Note over OP,SNOW: Investigate similar events
    OP->>APP: "show events like this"
    APP->>API: search by embedding
    API->>SNOW: VECTOR_COSINE_SIMILARITY top-k (WH_VECTOR)
    SNOW-->>APP: ranked similar events
